WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.000
DESK-HEAD: Following up on yesterday's CPI print, let's review how the flatten went.

2
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Priya: We got fully flat on two's tens about ten minutes before the release, as instructed.

3
00:00:40.000 --> 00:01:00.000
DESK-HEAD: Good. How did the five year position work out after we pulled back on size?

4
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:20.000
Priya: We trimmed most of it, held a small residual that actually worked in our favor after the print.

5
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:40.000
DESK-HEAD: That is a good outcome given how much the whisper number moved things.

6
00:01:40.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Priya: The number came in exactly two tenths above consensus, right where the whisper had it.

7
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:20.000
DESK-HEAD: Impressive that the whisper was that accurate this time, does not always work out that way.

8
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:40.000
Priya: Agreed, and the client call volume was heavy right after, just like we expected.

9
00:02:40.000 --> 00:03:00.000
DESK-HEAD: Good thing we had someone dedicated to phones, that would have been chaotic otherwise.

10
00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:20.000
Priya: Definitely, we handled about a dozen calls in the fifteen minutes after the release.

11
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:40.000
DESK-HEAD: For today, I want to keep a slightly more defensive posture given the volatility carried over.

12
00:03:40.000 --> 00:04:00.000
Priya: Makes sense, I will keep size a bit lighter than usual until things settle.

13
00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:20.000
DESK-HEAD: Good. Overall a clean execution on the flatten, nice work managing that under pressure.

14
00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:40.000
Priya: Thanks, the team handled it well, especially given how little notice we had.

15
00:04:40.000 --> 00:05:00.000
DESK-HEAD: Let's keep the same playbook ready in case we get another whisper like that this quarter.

16
00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:20.000
Priya: Agreed, I will write up a quick summary of what worked for next time.
